      "writtenOn": "2025-01-28T15:16:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "GCC\n```\n  movi v1.4s, 0\n  ins v1.s[0], v0.s[0]\n  frintn v1.4s, v1.4s\n  fcvtzu w0, s1\n  ret\n```\nClang\n```\n  movi v1.2d, #0000000000000000\n  mov v1.s[0], v0.s[0]\n  frintn v0.4s, v1.4s\n  fcvtzu w0, s0\n  ret\n```\n\nSo even with optimizations, this does pay the extra price of the splat. Not sure how much difference that makes. Mostly I was interested in seeing if, after optimizations, there was even a difference. It appears that the compiler doesn\u0027t see through the vector instruction and see that the effect of the `mov`s are being discarded.",
      "parentUuid": "a2215a08_11c64568",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "165450220ef432c4b40bba918b124b995f7ff0b3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c542971_4b9caabc",
        "filename": "src/opts/SkSwizzler_opts.inc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 5970
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-28T18:35:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Not sure how much difference that makes\n\nHow can I answer that question? Alternatively, are you leaning towards options 2, 3, or 4 for this?",
      "parentUuid": "a3f4cdbe_ff6f14a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "165450220ef432c4b40bba918b124b995f7ff0b3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ffb1d3d_bb268eb9",
        "filename": "src/opts/SkSwizzler_opts.inc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-04T18:48:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The least bad thing to do here is probably something like\n\n    #if GCC and GCC \u003c 8.5.0  // GCC lacked vrndns_f32 until 8.5.0\n        float32x4_t vN{n};\n        return vrndnq_f32(vN)[0];\n    #else\n        return vrndns_f32(n);\n    #endif\n    \nI\u0027m not sure if Skia already has a good \"this is GCC\" macro. If we were using autotools we\u0027d just add a feature check for the existence of `vrndns_f32` but we don\u0027t appear to have a nice thing like that already set up. Also, we do not want to test for places we know vrndns_f32 exists, we want to assume it exists and let builds fail where it doesn\u0027t and we haven\u0027t special cased that situation (vrndns_f32 use should always end up in the default case).",
      "parentUuid": "1c542971_4b9caabc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "165450220ef432c4b40bba918b124b995f7ff0b3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
